& [Threats]
  + T01 invalid P2 journal used to drive Git
  + T02 open tip differs from pinned HEAD
  + T03 PATH executable or executable-byte substitution
  + T04 ambient Git config replacement object lazy fetch prompt hook filter or external diff behavior
  + T05 repository root branch HEAD or object-format drift
  + T06 carrier identity is missing noncommit tag replacement or abbreviation
  + T07 carrier is root merge or has wrong parent
  + T08 commit tree identity is malformed or detached from raw commit content
  + T09 journal path is absent duplicated quoted aliased or traversing
  + T10 tree entry is symlink submodule tree executable nonblob or wrong mode
  + T11 blob object identity is malformed or substituted
  + T12 blob bytes exceed bounds truncate or differ from canonical record JSON plus LF
  + T13 observation ordering count or link binding differs
  + T14 command stdout stderr exit status count or resource bounds are ignored
  + T15 pre/post executable or repository replay drift is hidden
  + T16 receipt digest or authority is widened
  + T17 CLI output path filesystem write Git mutation network provider model MCP hook or broker surface appears
  + T18 Windows newline translation weakens raw blob equality
  + T19 human SOP bookend is mislabeled as a machine P2 record
  + T20 foreign workspace custody or self-signature leaks into publication

& [Mitigation]
  + strict P2-first validation hash-pinned absolute executable environment clearing no replacement/no fetch Git variables exact forty-hex object requests raw commit/tree/blob parsing bounded concurrent pipes exact canonical bytes pre/post equality domain-separated receipts static absence scans and disposable fixtures

& [Residual]
  + observation proves only the repository and exact instant contacted
  + no trust assertion is made about commit signer author operator intent remote hosting or future reachability
  + SWA-05 mutation recovery and publication replay remain separate
